Core Modeling (based on your DB)

orders.status = 'draft' means cart.
One active draft cart per customer.
Cart items map to order_items.
Add-to-cart should use product_variant_id (not product id), because price/stock are on variant.
Answer to your question

Product detail is not only for display.
It should return enough payload for add-to-cart:
product.id, name, slug
variants: id, sku, price, stock
Client sends variantId + quantity in mutation.
GraphQL Shape (recommended)

Queries:
products(first, after, search, categorySlug)
product(slug: String!)
myCart
Mutations:
addToCart(variantId: ID!, quantity: Int!): Cart
Optional next: updateCartItem, removeCartItem
Service Logic for addToCart

Find/create draft order for customer.
Validate variant exists and stock > 0.
If item already exists, increment quantity.
Save line with current variant price snapshot.
Recompute orders.total = sum(order_items.price * quantity).
Important DB Improvements before coding

Add unique draft cart constraint (one per customer):
Partial unique index on orders(customer_id) where status=draft.
Add indexes:
product_variants(product_id)
product_categories(product_id, category_id)
orders(customer_id, status)
order_items(order_id)
Consider order_items.product_variant_id as NOT NULL for cart/order history integrity (recommended for ecommerce).
